---
import TextPage from "../layouts/TextPage.astro";
import { BRAND_OWNERS, CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";
---

<TextPage
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`The terms for using ${SITE_NAME}: information only, asking prices, no guarantees.`}
  intro="By using this site you agree to these terms."
  updated="November 20, 2026"
>
  <h2>Information only</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} provides general information about used-electronics prices. It is not financial, legal or purchasing advice,
    and you decide for yourself whether and how to buy or sell.
  </p>

  <h2>Asking prices, no guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    The prices shown are asking prices from public listings, not sold prices. We do not verify that a listing is still
    available, accurate or honest, and our averages, deal scores and rankings are estimates that can contain errors or lag
    behind the market. We give no warranty about the accuracy, completeness or availability of anything on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Dealing with sellers</h2>
  <p>
    Any purchase or sale happens between you and the other person on Facebook or elsewhere. We are not a party to it and are not
    responsible for it. Take normal care: meet in public places, check items before paying and be careful with deposits and
    unusually low prices.
  </p>

  <h2>Trademarks and other sites</h2>
  <p>
    The names of {BRAND_OWNERS.replaceAll(" or ", " and ")}, and of their products, are trademarks of their owners. {SITE_NAME} is not affiliated with,
    endorsed by or sponsored by them. Listings and the content of other sites belong to their owners.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You may read and share the pages for personal use. Please do not overload the site with automated requests or try to disrupt
    it. We may change or remove any part of the site at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, {SITE_NAME} and its operator are not liable for any loss or damage that results from using or
    relying on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version; using the site after a change means you accept it.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>
</TextPage>
